{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The retained run reproduced the suspected mismatch: follower 2 submitted `(101,30)` but received `(202,30)`, follower 3’s context. Both leader-side requests were removed; three later heartbeat ticks produced no correction. I’ll make the formal check about preserving context through ReadIndex completion. This run does not establish a client timeout or stale read.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ns=Path('readindex_explore_test.go').read_text()\ns=s.replace('b, err := json.Marshal(v)','v[\\\"scenario\\\"] = \\\"forwarded_batch\\\"\\\\n        b, err := json.Marshal(v)')\ns=s.replace('ready[id] = append(ready[id], ud.ReadyToReads...)','''ready[id] = append(ready[id], ud.ReadyToReads...)\n        for _, rr := range ud.ReadyToReads {\n            emit(map[string]interface{}{\\\"event\\\":\\\"ready_result\\\", \\\"origin\\\":id, \\\"ctx\\\":fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%d/%d\\\", rr.SystemCtx.Low, rr.SystemCtx.High), \\\"index\\\":rr.Index})\n        }''')\ns=s.replace('peers[m.To].Handle(m)\\\\n            queue', '''peers[m.To].Handle(m)\n            if m.Type == pb.ReadIndex {\n                // Observe the actual admitted object before any response delivery.\n                ctx := pb.SystemCtx{Low:m.Hint, High:m.HintHigh}\n                if rs, ok := peers[m.To].raft.readIndex.pending[ctx]; ok {\n                    emit(map[string]interface{}{\\\"event\\\":\\\"admitted\\\", \\\"origin\\\":rs.from, \\\"ctx\\\":fmt.Sprintf(\\\"%d/%d\\\",rs.ctx.Low,rs.ctx.High), \\\"index\\\":rs.index, \\\"leader\\\":m.To})\n                }\n            }\n            queue''')\ns=s.replace('\\\"event\\\":\\\"prefix\\\", \\\"term\\\"','\\\"event\\\":\\\"prefix\\\", \\\"leader_ready\\\":peers[1].raft.isLeader() && peers[1].raft.hasCommittedEntryAtCurrentTerm(), \\\"term\\\"')\nPath('readindex_check_test.go').write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > build_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nold=json.load(open('readindex_explore.json'))\nsources=[dict(id='batch_context_expectation',file='internal/raft/readindex_test.go',start_line=135,end_line=176,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='follower_context_expectation',file='internal/raft/raft_test.go',start_line=2431,end_line=2449,kind='test_expectation')]\nbind='forwarded_read_confirmation'\nsrc=['read_batch','read_confirmation','read_forward_consume','peer_read_api','read_client_matching','read_node_producer','read_node_consumer']\nexpect=['batch_context_expectation','follower_context_expectation','read_client_matching']\ndef ground(ids,exp,why):\n return dict(source_ids=ids,expectation_ids=exp,binding_ids=[bind],derivation=why,applicability='Distinct nonzero read contexts, one operation per follower origin, stable term and membership, current-term entry committed before reads.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=[])\ng=ground(src,expect,'The queue retains the originating node and original SystemCtx for each confirmed read. The batch-confirmation test explicitly preserves each context while allowing its index to advance. Follower consumption passes response context through, and pendingReadIndex.addReady uses exact SystemCtx equality to find the originating batch. Therefore a forwarded completion must preserve the admitted request context; a later heartbeat context is not an alias for earlier requests.')\nclaim=dict(id='forwarded_read_context_obligation',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='When a leader completes queued forwarded ReadIndex requests after quorum confirmation, each response and resulting ReadyToRead must retain the SystemCtx of the corresponding admitted request at its originating follower, including earlier requests completed by a later heartbeat context.',source_ids=src+expect[:2],scope=dict(description='ReadIndex request identity across leader-side quorum batching and follower-side ReadyToRead delivery.',assumptions=['Stable term and voting membership during the requests.','Distinct nonzero SystemCtx values and known follower origins.','The leader has committed an entry in its current term.'],excluded=['Permanent liveness, client deadline breaches, and application read values.','Probability of random context collisions.']),pending=[],grounding=g)\nbinding=dict(id=bind,material_id='read_confirmation',symbol='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',start_line=1771,end_line=1790,description='Converts each confirmed readStatus into local readiness or a remote ReadIndexResp; remote branch uses the acknowledging message context.',pending=[])\nquestion=dict(question='Does quorum completion of multiple forwarded ReadIndex requests preserve each originating request context through the follower ReadyToRead endpoint?',source_ids=src+expect[:2],disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',importance='Losing the identity of a quorum-confirmed read prevents the client batch matcher from recognizing its completion.',activity_classes=['A1','A2','A7'],counterevidence=['The local completion branch uses s.ctx correctly.','The newer forwarded request receives its own context correctly.','Current-term and peer-membership admission protections remain enabled; no stale-term message is supplied.'],unknowns=['Formal check result and checker correspondence remain pending.','Client-level timeout consequences have not been executed.'])\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Exploration exposed a concrete mismatch at the protocol completion endpoint; encode only context preservation, whose requirement is supported by queue tests and the exact-context consumer.',question=question,obligation=claim,bindings=[binding])\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=['1af4aa07a48f4d08b60a72b95c415233'],answered='Retained exploration completed with exit 0. Prefix reached term 2, commit/applied index 4 at all nodes. Follower 2 context 101/30 was observed pending at leader 1, its two heartbeat sends were dropped, and follower 3 then requested 202/30. Real heartbeat responses caused ReadIndexResp 202/30 to both origins. Follower 2 ReadyToReads contained 202/30 at index 4, while the leader pending map was empty; three further leader ticks did not restore 101/30.',remaining=['Fresh direct execution and correspondence review are needed for a formal context-preservation result.','No NodeHost RequestState completion, client deadline breach, or stale application read was observed.'],rationale='The fixed exploration harness and its retained stdout expose the actual response messages and ReadyToReads. This is source-guided exploration, not retroactive formal confirmation. The new check adds independent origin-based correlation and admission observations.')\nsub=dict(action='check',rationale='Run a fresh direct check of original-context preservation using the successful real protocol prefix. Keep the newer request as an independent same-history control; do not infer client completion from ReadyToRead.',sources=sources,candidate=candidate,feedback=feedback,plan_path='readindex_plan.json',harness_path='readindex_check_test.go')\nlegal=ground(['peer_bootstrap','peer_bootstrap_entries','test_log_storage','peer_admission','term_admission','commit_quorum','election_config_guard','loss_permitted','peer_read_api','read_node_producer','read_client_matching'],['peer_read_api','loss_permitted'],'Launch builds initial membership and entries; TestLogDB stores every update before outbound delivery; committed bootstrap entries are applied and NotifyRaftLastApplied advances the real election guard. Node 1 ticks trigger its real election and current-term no-op replication. Requests enter Peer.ReadIndex and traverse Peer.Handle. Only the first two heartbeat sends are lost; all delivered messages retain FIFO order. Contexts are legal supplied Peer inputs with nonzero Low and caller-compatible High, not fabricated votes or confirmation state. The single-threaded driver drains each update synchronously and observes readiness before Commit clears it.')\nplan=dict(description='Three-node bootstrap and actual election; follower 2 request is queued after its heartbeat sends are lost, then follower 3 request obtains real quorum acknowledgment. Compare each follower ReadyToRead context against its actual leader-admitted context, correlated by scenario and originating node rather than by the compared context. Continue three fault-free heartbeat ticks, with no deadline claim.',harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},execution_package='internal/raft',description='Synchronous peer driver with TestLogDB storage, actual Launch/tick/read/Handle/GetUpdate/Commit calls, and two lost heartbeat sends.',semantic_changes=['No target logic changes.','In-memory storage and synchronous transport substitute for disk and networking; no crash or persistence failure is claimed.','Contexts are supplied directly to Peer.ReadIndex; NodeHost client workers are not instantiated.','Application of non-configuration entries is represented by sequential applied-index notification; no application value claim.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='prefix',event='prefix',conditions=[dict(field='leader_ready',op='eq',value=True)]),dict(alias='admission',event='admitted',conditions=[dict(field='scenario',op='eq',reference='prefix.scenario'),dict(field='leader',op='eq',value=1)])],legality=legal),monitors=[dict(id='ready_context_monitor',checker_id='ready_context_preserved',event='ready_result',binding_ids=[bind],grounding=g,admission_alias='admission',applicability_conditions=[dict(field='scenario',op='eq',reference='admission.scenario'),dict(field='origin',op='eq',reference='admission.origin')])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='ready_context_preserved',kind='event_assertion',trigger=dict(field='event',op='eq',value='ready_result'),assertion=dict(field='ctx',op='eq',reference='admission.ctx'),identity_fields=['scenario','origin'],description='The ReadyToRead context at a follower equals that follower operation\\\\'s leader-admitted context. There is exactly one request per originating follower.')],uncertainties=['The result is local completion-identity semantics, not a stale-read safety violation or a client deadline claim.','Three subsequent heartbeat ticks are a measured continuation only, not a permanent-stalling bound.'])\nPath('readindex_check.json').write_text(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPath('readindex_plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(plan,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-10_13-34-50-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission readindex_check.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
